  "memory": "# Dusk brand\nDusk is a lightweight dark-mode browser extension (a fast Dark Reader alternative). Audience: developers and heavy readers. Tone: calm, precise, quietly confident about performance.\n\n## Identity\n- Idea: dusk = the sun sinking below the horizon = turning the light down.\n- Mark: half sun resting on a horizon line. Wordmark: lowercase \"dusk.\" in Inter Tight Bold, the period in ember ($accent) as a setting sun.\n- Palette: ink $bg #0F0E17, violet $primary #A896FF, ember $accent #FF9466 (sparingly), paper #F6F3EE for \"light page\" depictions.\n- Type: Inter Tight (display), Inter (text), JetBrains Mono (numbers, labels).\n\n## Rules\n- No purple-to-blue gradients. Ember is the only warm colour and appears once per view.\n- Numbers come from the real benchmark (bench/out/run.log), never invented."
}